@@ -0,0 +1,108 @@
+# Gecko Presence 0.6.6 — Targeted security assessment
+
+**Assessment type:** source review + deterministic fuzz/property tests + loopback HTTP integration test  
+**Assessment date:** 2026-11-15  
+**Target:** Gecko Presence Android source, version 0.6.6  
+**Scope:** Gateway publisher, local artwork gallery, Imgur upload boundary, per-app profile storage, credential handling, WebView login boundary, Android manifest, and build/CI configuration.
+
+## Executive result
+
+**101 static security assertions passed**
+
+The new artwork upload and profile paths passed the available local checks. The Imgur uploader was exercised against a local loopback HTTP server; it did not contact Imgur or Discord. Gateway protocol and media-policy functions were fuzzed deterministically. This is a **targeted dynamic test pass**, not a full Android device penetration test and not a security certification.
+
+## Test evidence
+
+| Test | Cases / result | What it establishes |
+|---|---:|---|
+| `scripts/test-core.sh` | 6 suites passed | Existing source policies, token envelope behavior, Gateway payload rules, advanced profile validation, retry policy, and artwork media validation |
+| Gateway payload fuzz | 25,000 cases passed | UTF-8 payload serialization remains within the configured 4,096-byte limit for generated valid activity values |
+| Invalid-session retry fuzz | 10,000 cases passed | Retry delay remains within the one-to-five-second policy window |
+| Artwork malformed-input fuzz | 20,000 cases passed | Random malformed byte sequences do not bypass supported image-signature detection under the tested cases |
+| `scripts/test-imgur-upload-dynamic.sh` | Passed | Actual uploader sends multipart image data and Client-ID, does not forward cookies, refuses redirects, rejects unexpected returned hosts, caps response bytes, and rejects oversized files/invalid endpoints |
+| `scripts/security-audit.sh` | 101 assertions passed | Manifest, WebView, vault, gallery, uploader, profile persistence, and Gateway source contracts |
+| `scripts/verify-source.sh` | 98 source assertions passed | XML, build flavor, no-SDK/JNI, credential boundary, CI and source contract checks |
+
+The loopback HTTP test uses a small test-only JSON API stub because the host JVM does not provide Android's `org.json` implementation. The production uploader uses Android `org.json`. The integration test therefore validates HTTP/multipart behavior and uploader control flow, but not Android's JSON implementation itself.
+
+## Findings and residual risks
+
+| ID | Severity | Finding | Current mitigation / remaining risk |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| GP-01 | High residual | Discord web-session credential is a bearer credential with broad account access. | AES-256-GCM at rest with Android Keystore key, no clipboard/paste path, no token logging, explicit connect. Rooted-device/runtime instrumentation may still read it from process memory. |
+| GP-02 | Medium | Anonymous image upload makes selected images publicly reachable. | Upload requires explicit confirmation, names Imgur as destination, and warns about public visibility. Users must not upload private or identifying images. Remote deletion is not implemented. |
+| GP-03 | Medium | Discord user-session Gateway flow is undocumented/unsupported. | Payload fields follow the observed Kizzy implementation; protocol behavior can change or be rejected. Account enforcement risk remains outside Gecko's control. |
+| GP-04 | Low | Per-app activity profiles are stored in app-private SharedPreferences without encryption. | These records contain user-authored presence text and image URLs, not Discord credentials. Android app sandbox and backup exclusion protect at rest; rooted-device extraction remains possible. |
+| GP-05 | Medium | Full Android runtime hardening is not verified. | No APK was built in this environment; Frida, Objection, MobSF, JADX review of the built APK, rooted-device testing, and Samsung A04 dynamic tests remain outstanding. |
+| GP-06 | Low | Uploaded image remains on Imgur after deleting the local gallery entry. | UI explicitly states this. Remote deletion would require retaining and safely managing Imgur delete hashes, which is not implemented. |
+
+## Attack-surface review
+
+### 1. Gallery import and local storage
+
+- Imports use Android's document picker and copy the selected bytes immediately into Gecko's app-private `filesDir`.
+- Maximum file size is 8 MiB; maximum dimensions are 8,192 × 8,192 and 40 megapixels; maximum gallery size is 40 images / 64 MiB.
+- Accepted formats are JPEG, PNG, and WebP based on file signatures, not just the provider MIME label.
+- Filenames are generated UUIDs. Canonical-path checks prevent metadata from redirecting reads outside the gallery directory.
+- SHA-256 deduplication avoids duplicate local copies. File reads before upload verify stored size and hash against metadata.
+- SVG, GIF, HEIC, animated formats, and arbitrary document types are rejected.
+
+### 2. Imgur upload boundary
+
+- Production upload endpoint is hard-coded to `https://api.imgur.com/3/image`.
+- The only authorization header is `Client-ID {user supplied public client id}`. No Discord session token, Imgur account token, cookie, or Client Secret is attached.
+- Redirect following is disabled. Connection/read timeouts are bounded. The response is capped at 64 KiB.
+- Returned URLs must be HTTPS on the exact `i.imgur.com` host, port 443/default, without userinfo or fragment.
+- UI requires a separate confirmation before upload and explains the image becomes publicly reachable.
+- Test-only endpoint injection is restricted to loopback hosts and is not used by the production UI path.
+
+### 3. Per-app profile storage and application
+
+- Package names are validated before persistence/read/delete.
+- Profile JSON reads are capped at 16 KiB; activity values are checked against the same activity model used by the publisher.
+- Supported fields: type, name, details, state, stream URL, large/small image, tooltips, up to two buttons, timestamps, priority override, enable state, and optional account status.
+- A disabled profile does not publish for its package. Account status overrides the global setting only when that package wins arbitration.
+- Profiles are preferences, not credentials. They are not exported through the app's external components.
+
+### 4. Gateway transport
+
+- WebSocket client and session frame size are capped at 64 KiB. Text frames are checked again by UTF-8 byte count before JSON parsing.
+- WebSocket connect/upgrade and the subsequent HELLO handshake each have a 15-second timeout; established sessions do not inherit a short idle socket timeout.
+- Outbound Gateway payloads are validated against the 4,096-byte limit before send.
+- Writes are serialized, updates coalesced, and the configured minimum presence interval is applied.
+- Heartbeat ACK timeout, reconnect backoff, invalid-session delay, close-code policy, and explicit disconnect are handled in the publisher.
+- No frame content, token, resume URL, server close reason, or exception message is logged.
+
+### 5. WebView credential import and vault
+
+- The WebView login is not OAuth2; it reads the first-party Discord web-session value only after explicit user action.
+- The WebView is isolated, top-level navigation is origin-filtered, JavaScript native bridge is absent, TLS errors fail closed, file access is disabled, third-party cookies are disabled, and session data cleanup is retried after process death.
+- Credential ciphertext is stored in private preferences; AES key is non-exportable through the Android Keystore API.
+- This reduces accidental leakage but does not make a session bearer credential safe on a compromised device.
+
+## Verification gaps — do not interpret as passed
+
+- No Gradle Android build or APK artifact was produced in this environment. The archive's build toolchain still needs a real Gradle 8.10.2/JDK 17/Android SDK Platform 35 run in CI.
+- No installation or runtime test was run on Samsung A04 / Android 14.
+- No live Discord login, Gateway Identify, Resume, Presence Update acceptance, or rendering was performed.
+- No real Imgur upload was performed. The local integration server was used instead.
+- No Frida/Objection hooks, rooted-device test, MobSF, JADX review of a signed APK, or Play Integrity test was performed.
+- The local temporary-stub compilation checks do not verify binary linkage against Android SDK 35, Ktor 2.3.13, or the actual Android Gradle Plugin.
+
+## Reproduction
+
+```sh
+bash scripts/test-core.sh
+bash scripts/test-imgur-upload-dynamic.sh
+bash scripts/security-audit.sh
+bash scripts/verify-source.sh
+```
+
+For Android CI/build verification:
+
+```sh
+gradle --no-daemon :app:testSecureDebugUnitTest :app:testAutomationDebugUnitTest
+gradle --no-daemon :app:assembleSecureDebug :app:assembleAutomationDebug
+```
+
+The Gateway user-session flow remains a compatibility-sensitive, unsupported platform interaction. No technique to hide it from Discord or bypass platform enforcement is included.
